# WF-010 – Platform Health Monitoring & Diagnostics

## 1. Purpose

The Platform Health Monitoring & Diagnostics workflow continuously monitors the operational health, availability, and performance of the Enterprise AI Orchestration Platform.

The workflow collects health information from infrastructure components, AI services, vector databases, external integrations, and application services to provide proactive monitoring, rapid fault detection, and operational visibility.

---

## 2. Business Scenario

Enterprise AI platforms consist of multiple distributed services.

A failure in any component may affect user requests.

Examples include:

- Gemini API unavailable
- Qdrant offline
- Firestore unavailable
- MCP Server failure
- OpenSearch timeout
- GCS unavailable
- High response latency

The Operations team requires a centralized mechanism to detect issues before they impact users.

---

## 3. Trigger

The workflow is initiated by:

- Scheduled health checks
- Administrator request
- Monitoring system
- Startup validation
- Readiness probe
- Liveness probe

Example:

```text
Check platform health.
```

---

