## 7. Detailed Execution Flow

### Step 1 – Receive Health Request

The administrator or monitoring system invokes the Health API.

---

### Step 2 – Component Discovery

The Monitoring Service identifies all configured platform components.

---

### Step 3 – Service Health Checks

Each component is checked independently.

Examples:

- Gemini connectivity
- Qdrant availability
- Firestore connectivity
- OpenSearch status
- MCP Server status
- GCS accessibility

---

### Step 4 – Performance Metrics

The platform gathers operational metrics such as:

- Response time
- Error rate
- Request latency
- Memory usage
- CPU utilization
- Queue length

---

### Step 5 – Aggregate Results

The Health Agent aggregates individual component results into an overall platform health status.

Example:

```text
Overall Status : HEALTHY

Gemini        : UP
Qdrant        : UP
Firestore     : UP
OpenSearch    : DEGRADED
MCP Server    : UP
```

---

### Step 6 – Generate Diagnostics

The platform generates recommendations for any unhealthy or degraded services.

---

### Step 7 – Return Health Report

The monitoring report is returned to the administrator or monitoring system.

---

## 8. Component Responsibilities

| Component | Responsibility |
|-----------|----------------|
| Health API | Exposes health endpoints |
| Monitoring Service | Executes health checks |
| Health Agent | Aggregates health information |
| Qdrant | Reports vector database status |
| Firestore | Reports metadata database status |
| OpenSearch | Reports lexical search status |
| Gemini API | Reports AI service availability |
| MCP Server | Reports tool integration status |
| Logging Service | Records monitoring events |

---

## 9. Error Handling

| Failure | System Behaviour |
|----------|------------------|
| Health endpoint unavailable | Return service unavailable |
| Component timeout | Mark component as DEGRADED |
| Component failure | Mark component as DOWN |
| Partial failure | Return degraded platform status |

---

## 10. Security Considerations

- Require administrator authentication.
- Restrict health information exposure.
- Mask sensitive configuration values.
- Audit administrative access.
- Protect monitoring endpoints.

---

## 11. Performance Considerations

- Execute health checks in parallel.
- Cache expensive health results.
- Configure timeout thresholds.
- Minimize monitoring overhead.

---

## 12. Future Enhancements

- Prometheus integration.
- Grafana dashboards.
- Distributed tracing.
- Automated alerting.
- SLA reporting.
- Predictive health analytics.

---

## 13. Success Criteria

The workflow is considered successful when:

- All configured components are checked.
- Platform status is computed correctly.
- Diagnostics are generated.
- Results are available to administrators and monitoring systems.

